7.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {B2}
White’s immediate target is the black C1–C2 group. After the initial position C1–C2 has the two outside liberties B1 and B2. Playing B2 removes the B2 liberty and leaves the group with the single remaining liberty B1.
If Black does not answer on B1 White plays B1 next move and captures C1–C2 outright, because the group is then surrounded by White at B2, D1, D2, C3 and B1. If Black tries to save the group by playing B1 at once the group is still connected to A2–B3–B4 and now shares the liberties A1, A3 and A4 with the rest of the Black stones. White can then take the rest of the liberties in a net, e.g. A3 followed by A4, and the enlarged Black group has no move to avoid capture. The move therefore creates an unavoidable capture sequence for White and is the natural killing first move.

