1.W ≠ D3 is met at once by 2.B D3 and the D1–D2 string is removed, so the only non-losing first play is the forced self-save 1.W D3. After 1.W D3

G_W = {D1,D2,D3,C3,C4}
lives on D4,C5 and D4,C5 are suicide for Black.

The only Black material that can be touched is

C1–C2 : B1,B2
A2    : A1,A3,B2
B3–B4 : A3,A4,B2

which are legally joined by 2.B B2. After 1.W D3 2.B B2

G_B = {A2,B2,B3,B4,C1,C2}
has outside liberties A1,A3,A4,B1, so B2 gains liberties on the connection and is not suicide.

The B1/B2 net is therefore a snap-back:

* 1.W B1 → C1–C2 is in atari on B2 but 2.B B2 is legal, merges the three fragments into G_B with ≥3 outside liberties and leaves W B1 with the single liberty A1;
* 1.W B2 → mutual atari on B1, 2.B B1 captures W B2 and connects C1–C2 to B1, classic snap-back;
* 1.W A1,A3,A4 are immediate self-atari or are met by 2.B B2 which restores G_B with ≥3 unfillable outside liberties.

No first White move makes a Black group one liberty with a defending point illegal under normal suicide rules, and Black can always either connect at B2 and keep the merged A2–B3–B4–C1–C2 material alive on A1,A3,A4,B1, or capture the over-playing White stone, or liberate C1–C2 by 2.B D3 against any 1.W ≠ D3. The forced survival move 1.W D3 does not initiate a forced capture, so there is no first move that forces a kill against perfect defence.
